  "question": "The SMRT paper reports its active-mode comparison in Figure 4b for the same snowpack as the passive panel. Produce that curve: co-polarised backscatter against incidence angle from 15 to 60 degrees at 37 GHz, with DMRT QCA-CP short range. Take the snowpack properties from the paper, then run the model and plot it.",
  "answer": "I've reproduced Figure 4b from the SMRT paper by running the model with the exact snowpack parameters reported in section 08 [smrt-v1#08]: sphere radius $r=0.1$ mm, density $\\rho=300$ kg/m³, stickiness $\\tau=0.5$, and temperature $T=256$ K, using DMRT QCA-CP short range with sticky hard spheres [model:smrt@1.5.1].\n\nThe plot shows co-polarized backscatter ($\\sigma_{HH}$ and $\\sigma_{VV}$) against incidence angle from 15° to 60° at 37 GHz. Both polarizations exhibit a monotonic decrease with angle, ranging from approximately -17.3 dB at 15° to -22.2 dB (HH) and -21.5 dB (VV) at 60°, consistent with the reference results where differences were within 0.65 dB RMS [smrt-v1#08].\n\n<chart on screen>",
